^{:go/end 154} (go/func ^:go/nosplit mutexPreferLowLatency "mutexPreferLowLatency reports if this mutex prefers low latency at the risk\nof performance collapse. If so, we can allow all waiting threads to spin on\nthe state word rather than go to sleep.\n\nTODO: We could have the waiting Ms each spin on their own private cache line,\nespecially if we can put a bound on the on-CPU time that would consume.\n\nTODO: If there's a small set of mutex values with special requirements, they\ncould make use of a more specialized lock2/unlock2 implementation. Otherwise,\nwe're constrained to what we can fit within a single uintptr with no\nadditional storage on the M for each lock held.\n" ^bool [^{:tag (* mutex)} l]
  (switch l
    (default
      (return false))
    (case [(addr (.-lock sched))]
      ;; We often expect sched.lock to pass quickly between Ms in a way that
      ;; each M has unique work to do: for instance when we stop-the-world
      ;; (bringing each P to idle) or add new netpoller-triggered work to the
      ;; global run queue.
      (return true))))



